86510686}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7526651e-3bb1-5a8c-b6a7-9e835e617845" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=4x-4\\sqrt{x}$ at the point $(25,80).$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x-4\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x-4{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =4-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=25$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=25} & =4-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point $(25,80)$ is\n\n$$\nm={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=25}=\\frac{18}{5}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510690 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df72c75e-38d9-59fd-95c6-a6a89557fe6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df72c75e-38d9-59fd-95c6-a6a89557fe6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510696} :answer-field/id #uuid "70fb7748-33e1-502e-9aea-e98de3cc4b31" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510688}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88fecdbc-7bc6-55ea-9ea8-19f24b070e65" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=9\\sqrt{x}-2{x}^{3/4}$ at the point $(256,16).$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9\\sqrt{x}-2{x}^{3/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{x}^{1/2}-2{x}^{3/4}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}{x}^{-1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-1/4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=256$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=256} & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point $(256,16)$ is\n\n$$\nm={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=256}=-\\frac{3}{32}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f99bc2f0-dc2e-52dc-9a0f-88e468f57bb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f99bc2f0-dc2e-52dc-9a0f-88e468f57bb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510699} :answer-field/id #uuid "e512f17f-c103-5c3c-82bb-5f6973f5c51f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510697}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "99a60241-72e6-5737-aea9-72c487d2682d" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=3x-6\\sqrt{x}$ at the point $(25,45).$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-6\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-6{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =3-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=25$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=25} & =3-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point $(25,45)$ is\n\n$$\nm={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=25}=\\frac{12}{5}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aacfe591-5179-533b-a4db-353ac1025958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aacfe591-5179-533b-a4db-353ac1025958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510693} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef8bb82f-c22d-5cef-a814-8ca96adebf89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510698}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a7b32659-efdb-5f24-a94b-157e0fbb1fed" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=4\\sqrt{x}-8{x}^{3/4}$ at the point $(256,-448).$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\sqrt{x}-8{x}^{3/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{1/2}-8{x}^{3/4}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-8\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}{x}^{-1/4} \\\\  & =2{x}^{-1/2}-6{x}^{-1/4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=256$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=256} & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point $(256,-448)$ is\n\n$$\nm={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=256}=-\\frac{11}{8}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve With Fractional Powers at a Given Point"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092375 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092081 :question/id #uuid "1957007f-eabd-5d40-8f59-ff635ea1d539" :question/math-academy-id "e-602" :question/problem "![](images/83/834eff403ac2a6f696e104ec914cac1b951f8a6d989e11c0e9f2576ac9e7f0d8.png)\n\nFind an integral expression for the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-t, \\quad y= \\dfrac{2}{3} t^{3/2}, \\qquad t\\in[0,1].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} \\sqrt{ \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2 + \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\:\\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2})={t}^{1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{(-1)}^{2}+{({t}^{1/2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b03546f-6c79-53b9-b284-fb23ae4dba52" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050217 :topic/math-academy-id 760 :topic/title "The Arc Length of a Planar Curve"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050531 :topic/math-academy-id 798 :topic/title "Differentiating Parametric Curves"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "980c32be-9337-5148-aafb-c9804c249b8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9t^{4} + 12t^{2} + 4}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089616} {:answer/id #uuid "c7597a52-6382-5d77-a48e-c688a94aa2da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{t^{4} + 4t^{2} + 2}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089617} {:answer/id #uuid "05072a23-fdb5-5ea9-91d2-634bdb351f17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{t^{4} + 4t^{2} + 1}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089618} {:answer/id #uuid "150cbc59-2ca7-54ec-a6a8-67ca6cba9c5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{t^{4} + t^{2} + 1}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089619} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb7b801-40e5-58de-b29f-fe621d66b0b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9t^{4} + 16t^{2} + 4}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089620}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4cc9cbdc-b53f-5d3e-98b2-5cf0e50befd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089615}] :question/id #uuid "f0d23e0d-f38a-562a-8c27-86c2428291ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-15172" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x = t^{2} + 1, y = t^{3} + 2t$\nfrom $t =-1$ to $t = 1$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a124acdc-e495-5b11-b2b6-753bf6e46659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\displaystyle \\int_{-3}^{2}\\sqrt{2t^{4} - t^{2} + 2t + 1}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091157} {:answer/id #uuid "b1926fa9-7a78-5623-aaed-effce755523c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{-3}^{2}\\sqrt{2t^{2} + t + 1}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091158} {:answer/id #uuid "d3611a38-c0b5-5dc9-9132-078542d94502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{-3}^{2}\\sqrt{t^{4} - t^{2} + t + 1}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091159} {:answer/id #uuid "2fde0d28-04a8-5bdc-956f-de766ab86529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\displaystyle \\int_{-3}^{2}\\sqrt{t^{4} - t^{2} + 2t + 2}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091160} {:answer/id #uuid "57d3f5ba-4367-5524-a843-57e49b68ed77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\displaystyle \\int_{-3}^{2}\\sqrt{t^{2} + 2t + 2}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091161}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c7484595-bd71-5a88-ac55-560af2ce4f19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091156}] :question/id #uuid "767ca9bf-bda6-519c-b045-66d55d563e0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-81437" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2c96a0fc119984b83ba68a0cfc50540563a3ea76cc887d3e184238250773e91b.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x = t^{2} + 2t + 1, y = \\frac{2}{3}t^{3} - 2t$\nfrom $t =-3$ to $t = 2$ (shown above)?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256770 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1691c723-a29f-5657-aee7-eec47906ae55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{8{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+20{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253864} {:answer/id #uuid "52ebc669-036d-52bd-bd42-f8a9effb2d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{{t}^{6}+{t}^{4}+{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254393} {:answer/id #uuid "aea928a3-cf09-5314-9b87-9ec1f92f214b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+40{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255207} {:answer/id #uuid "b39d0d7c-49b9-5298-8296-ac358a89bec4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{4{t}^{6}+3{t}^{4}+4{t}^{3}+5}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255251} {:answer/id #uuid "ff64285b-3a4e-5ddc-aa99-b508b397f090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+49{t}^{4}+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aea928a3-cf09-5314-9b87-9ec1f92f214b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+40{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255207} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ac33bf7-e329-5540-9b40-ace253188539" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255997}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ac06717-3d6e-5cb8-bb53-88e2680a811e" :question/math-academy-id "q-123005" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x={t}^{3}-8,\\,y={t}^{4}+5t$\nfrom $t=-2$ to $t=3$ ?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-8)=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}+5t)=4{t}^{3}+5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{{(3{t}^{2})}^{2}+{(4{t}^{3}+5)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+16{t}^{6}+40{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+40{t}^{3}+25}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "070a4318-5841-5f5c-8d72-6fb59872fc0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}-12}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253722} {:answer/id #uuid "17d49195-6be3-5ce7-aa2a-921578f62915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{36{t}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253877} {:answer/id #uuid "3741fd0d-810d-5265-b32c-6114a62fde8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{6{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254148} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd7ccb4-e388-5676-9be3-2b14b685baf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{36{t}^{2}+5t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254331} {:answer/id #uuid "528db892-4fe7-531e-81df-1965b9853c97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+5}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17d49195-6be3-5ce7-aa2a-921578f62915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{36{t}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253877} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9c515a7-5b1f-551b-a793-9f6e12bfd819" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256279}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6c68291-2bb7-56b1-a306-1312ff237a63" :question/math-academy-id "q-123019" :question/problem "![](images/0a/0a58808ee9b20e201d1ea8a31683f742e02f739127640de2fea87ce4757e7901.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=3{t}^{2},\\,y=5t$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$ (shown above)?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})=6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t)=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{(6t)^{2}+(5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{36{t}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2107bda6-d473-50dd-ba60-ad2a320b0aed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{27{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}-t+6}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253962} {:answer/id #uuid "3421b0d5-8f17-526e-9dba-9537c508fcc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}-20t+5}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254121} {:answer/id #uuid "6c853f8d-b33e-5895-ba0b-c7a9e2102da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{85{t}^{4}-20t+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254634} {:answer/id #uuid "8799eb05-fe1e-5cc8-b350-130c501b0286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+{t}^{2}-5t+6}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254873} {:answer/id #uuid "d79fac35-f1e8-5450-97f3-86f17fbbb483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{81{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}-20t+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d79fac35-f1e8-5450-97f3-86f17fbbb483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{81{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}-20t+25}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255579} :answer-field/id #uuid "132e3016-73cb-5474-ae06-aa55eeff7889" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255950}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a0cda492-f891-5b24-90a6-900da47a3f8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-123025" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=3{t}^{3}+5,\\,y={t}^{2}-5t$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=2$ ?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{3}+5)=9{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-5t)=2t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{(9{t}^{2})^{2}+(2t-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{81{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}-20t+25}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351299 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40667602-c7d2-52f3-b515-00979eaf90c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{4+t+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349032} {:answer/id #uuid "514b71c4-dc4b-550b-a85a-0e54a3f5b5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{4+4t+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349185} {:answer/id #uuid "5898362e-f963-559f-b809-786b12c62c78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4t+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349260} {:answer/id #uuid "784441b4-8a2c-50a3-b06e-746d478ecd7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{t+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349554} {:answer/id #uuid "caa71d58-f8d1-5f06-9145-4ddcc7adf731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caa71d58-f8d1-5f06-9145-4ddcc7adf731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350231} :answer-field/id #uuid "7706adee-7a3b-5175-ab48-f3203b4530f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350913}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc4af2ef-5b85-5a46-b1fb-ff4ea6d0758d" :question/math-academy-id "q-81377" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=t-1,\\,y={t}^{2}+2$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=2$ ?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2)=2t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{{(1)}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "173b2b5c-5428-506b-9f15-da54e1e7da07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348641} {:answer/id #uuid "1af0386f-90d9-5a79-afed-aa45754d349a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348677} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce5f7a3-81c2-5b76-a5e7-4963090954d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348699} {:answer/id #uuid "2c69be06-5fa9-5750-ba1a-4f53458bc229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348835} {:answer/id #uuid "d64b585a-e82a-5026-900a-c28a246b6b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{3{t}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ce5f7a3-81c2-5b76-a5e7-4963090954d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348699} :answer-field/id #uuid "b11f3cba-eadf-5d36-86ff-2f0552d4e5e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351010}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f078660-763f-536d-9faf-52311fdcfddf" :question/math-academy-id "q-81380" :question/problem "![](images/12/120220c7c1a24c68c1a9282548efcf62c34fd110bd11911799a2a83409f257ab.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x={t}^{3}+1,\\,y=3t$\nfrom $t=-2$ to $t=0$ (shown above)?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+1)=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2})^{2}+(3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e2720b5-b7ef-506c-86d6-fa144d1dbad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}-2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\," :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394705} {:answer/id #uuid "962d9602-db26-5929-a1c1-0bd2caac4e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{3{t}^{2}+2t-1}\\,\\text{d}t\\," :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394706} {:answer/id #uuid "2589a138-5496-5db8-b982-4b36bc678287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-12t+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\," :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394707} {:answer/id #uuid "d18f1c16-5f34-5e7a-9